TITLE The Capital One Café, Post and Kearny | October 2026. Two laptops, two coffees.
PAUSE 4
JASON: Hmm. [1.2]
ERIC: What.
JASON: None of these recruiters are responding, man. [0.6]
JASON: Should I be doing more projects?
ERIC: You should do something at least.
JASON: How about My Cookbook?
ERIC: I mean, sure. [0.5]
ERIC: You keep saying that but not doing anything about it.
JASON (sad): I'm just a brick man, I just use AI without thinking.
PAUSE 5
JASON: Did you finish your interview?
ERIC: Yeah, it was the third round. [0.5]
ERIC: I kind of got grilled, though.
JASON: I see. That's really good, man. [1.4]
JASON (open): Dang, third round? Where's my first?
ERIC: The job market is cooked, man. Just keep trying.
PAUSE 6
JASON: Do you ever think about what you'd do if you were me?
ERIC: I'd have sent five emails by now.
JASON: Hmm.
ERIC: Bro, just send it. Then pick lunch. [0.6]
ERIC: You have ninety seconds or I pick.
JASON: Chipotle.
ERIC: Ok now use this decisiveness on your emails instead. [1.6]
ERIC: So?
JASON (sad): Man, why do I even send these emails.
ERIC: Seventy seconds.
PAUSE 6
JASON: Chipotle.
PAUSE 2
CARD Eric got an offer that week. Jason was sitting across the table.
